{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791055132,"nonce":"UaO70uFJgVAcMrJxOtcWK3JtJ50=","message":"The CSS half is now wired: LayoutRenderer::compute_layout syncs RenderProps.letter_spacing into each text node's measure context before measuring, writing only on a change so a steady frame does not re-measure every text node.\n\nWider finding from the same seam, deliberately NOT fixed: nothing syncs props into the measure context at all, so CSS font-size and line-height are equally invisible to the measurer (both are set in stylesheet/apply.rs and neither reaches TextMeasureContext). Letter-spacing was safe to wire because the context value is always 0.0 today, so only elements that explicitly set it change. font-size and line-height would change measured sizes for every element carrying those properties, which is a visible layout change across the framework and wants a deliberate decision rather than being folded into this fix.","files":null}]}